<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46984" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suppŏsĭtīcĭus</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subpŏs-</span></b> )
		or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tĭus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		suppono, I. B., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>put in the place of</i> another, <i>substituted.</i> * </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: Hermes supposititius sibi ipsi, <i>is his own substitute</i>, i. e. <i>he needs no
				one to replace him in combat</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 5,
				24, 8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In partic., <i>not genuine</i>, <i>false</i>, <i>supposititious</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mater,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 2, 8, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">explorator,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 4, 7, 71</span></i>
			. </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
